# Commodore  

  

## Overview  

  

Commodore is the most junior flag officer rank within Eagle Fleet. Officers holding this rank are entrusted with senior leadership responsibilities and often serve as commanders of task groups, department heads, or senior members of the Admiralty.  

  

The rank represents the transition from ship command to fleet-level leadership and administration.  

  

## Rank Information  

  

| Category | Value |  

|----------|--------|  

| Rank | Commodore |  

| Abbreviation | CDRE |  

| Grade | Flag Officer |  

| Superior Rank | [[04 Rear Admiral]] |  

| Junior Rank | [[06 Captain]] |  

| Typical Posting | Task Group Command, Fleet Staff, Department Director |  

  

## Responsibilities  

  

- Commanding task groups and special operations  

- Leading fleet departments and directorates  

- Supporting fleet-wide planning and coordination  

- Supervising ship commanders within assigned commands  

- Developing policy and operational guidance  

- Representing the Admiralty on assigned matters  

  

## Authority  

  

A Commodore exercises authority over all personnel, vessels, and resources assigned to their command and serves as a senior leader within the fleet command structure.  

  

## Typical Assignments  

  

- Task Group Commander  

- Department Director  

- Chief of Staff  

- Deputy Task Force Commander  

- Strategic Planning Officer  

- Fleet Administration Officer  

  

